origin.originalSolution:
Since $\mathbf{u}=\vec{OC}$ and $\mathbf{v}=\vec{AC}$:
$$\begin{align*}
\vec{OA} + \vec{AC} &= \vec{OC} \\
\vec{OA} + \mathbf{v} &= \mathbf{u} \\
\vec{OA} &= \mathbf{u}-\mathbf{v}
\end{align*}$$
Since $AB$ is a diameter with centre $O$, $O$ is the midpoint of $AB$, so:
$$\begin{align*}
\vec{OB} &= -\vec{OA} \\
&= -(\mathbf{u}-\mathbf{v}) \\
&= \mathbf{v}-\mathbf{u}
\end{align*}$$
Then:
$$\begin{align*}
\vec{BC} &= \vec{BO}+\vec{OC} \\
&= -\vec{OB}+\mathbf{u} \\
&= -(\mathbf{v}-\mathbf{u})+\mathbf{u} \\
&= 2\mathbf{u}-\mathbf{v}
\end{align*}$$

